 – a strong operational dimension – derived from ISO 31000 – to enhance operational risk and opportunity management, identifying and mitigating threats and vulnerabilities, including single points of failure;
 – a reporting dimension (bottom up and top down), which contains procedures for the status reporting of the ERM system and the risk/opportunity situation; and
